.docname {First steps}
.include {docs}

This page walks you through a first session: placing a pattern, running it, and undoing a mistake.

## The Game of Life in one paragraph

The board is a grid of cells, each either alive or dead. Every generation, each cell counts its eight neighbours. A dead cell with exactly three live neighbours is born; a live cell with two or three live neighbours survives; every other cell dies or stays dead. This rule is written `B3/S23` (*birth on 3, survival on 2 or 3*), and gol-bevy can run [other rules](simulation.qd#rules) too.

## 1. Place a glider

1. Click **Stamp** (the third drawing tool in the toolbar) or press .keybinding {3}. The pattern palette opens on the left. Click **Glider** in it.
2. Move the mouse over the board. A translucent preview shows where the glider will land.
3. Click to place it. Click again elsewhere to place more.

Press .keybinding {Z} to rotate the stamp and .keybinding {F} to flip it. The preview always shows the orientation that will be placed.

## 2. Run it

Press .keybinding {Space} or click **Play**. The glider travels diagonally, one cell every four generations. Press .keybinding {Space} again to pause, and .keybinding {J} to advance a single generation.

The status bar at the bottom shows whether the board is running, the generation, the number of living cells, and the rule.

## 3. Draw your own cells

Press .keybinding {C} to drop the stamp and return to the **Draw** tool. Now drag with the left mouse button to bring cells to life. Drag with the right button to erase.

## 4. Undo a mistake

Press .keybinding {U} or .keybinding {Mod+Z}. Undo restores the board and pauses playback, so you can look at what you got back. A whole drag counts as one edit. Redo with .keybinding {Mod+Shift+Z}.

## 5. Try a random board

Press .keybinding {R} to fill about a quarter of the board at random, then .keybinding {Space} to watch it settle. Press .keybinding {X} to clear the board.

## Moving around

- Scroll over the board to zoom, or use **− / +** in the status bar.
- Pan by middle-button dragging, or with .keys {W, A, S, D} or the arrow keys.
- Press .keybinding {V}, or click **Fit board** (the corner brackets at the right of the status bar), to fit the whole board back into view.

## Getting help in the app

Press .keybinding {/} or click **Help** to see every shortcut. Hover over or focus a button to see its shortcut hint.

